Z||000000||MATT*GT||11-13-2001||08:19 PM||||I have a 86 GT with a bad vibration that starts at 50mph and is the worst at 60 to 65mph.The car has been to three shops and all have said the ball joints and tie rods are ok I also had new tires put on and it did not seem to help. The problem did get worse after installing the vented front brake kit from the Fiero store. Any help would be great<BR>Thanks, Matt Larson||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||11-13-2001||08:45 PM||||Did you check your wheel bearings, if you reused them? Were they packed with (wheel bearing) grease correctly? Did you install the vented rotors yourself or have a mechanic do it? If the bearings were'nt tightened correctly they could cause vibration and they will self destruct fairly quick. Hope this helps. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MATT*GT||11-13-2001||09:15 PM||||I did install the brake kit myself and the kit came with new wheel bearings. I did pack them with greese and tightened them to what i thought was right but how tight should thay be? Thanks for your reply.||||reg||1
